hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"991","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani told us, Yazid, meaning Ibn Zurayi, told us, al-Hajjaj told us, and Ahmad ibn Abdah told us, Yazid bin Zuray’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj Al-Ahwal Al-Bahili, Qatada told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked Peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the authority of a man who neglects prayer or neglects it. He said: “The expiation for it is that he prays it when he remembers it.” And Ibn Abdah said: On the authority of Qatada, and he also said: That he should pray it whenever he remembers it."
"992","Abu Musa told us, Abdul Ala told us, Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Whoever forgets a prayer, or falls asleep during it, its expiation is for him to pray it when he remembers it.” Ali bin Khashram told us, Issa told us, on the authority of Sa`id, with this chain of narration in a similar manner."
"993","Salam bin Junada told us, Waki` told us, on the authority of Hammam bin Yahya, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it. There is no expiation for it except that.”"
